  "disputed_property": "https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#yieldStrength",
  "source": {
    "source_clause": "I2.4.2 — longitudinally framed plating",
    "frozen_source_text": "In the case of longitudinally-framed plating (Omega <= 20 deg), when b >= s, the net thickness is t_net = 500*s*sqrt((AF*PPF_p*P_avg)/sigma_y)/(1 + s/(2*l)) [mm]. When b < s, the net thickness is t_net = 500*s*sqrt((AF*PPF_p*P_avg)/sigma_y)*sqrt(2*b/s - (b/s)^2)/(1 + s/(2*l)) [mm].",
    "source_applicability_review": "Longitudinal framing Omega<=20 degrees; formula branches b>=s and b<s retain the same missing property-owner assignments.",
    "original_pdf": "/Users/sadisfaction570/Desktop/Journal 1/NLTL_v2/MVP/RELEVANT FILES/ur-i2rev4.pdf",
    "original_pdf_sha256": "2142453d2965997a772f451982278e622413273048097924173216bd278df9a7",
    "full_source_text": "/Users/sadisfaction570/Desktop/Journal 1/NLTL_v2/MVP/evaluation_audit/source_review/IACS_I2_full.txt",
    "full_source_sha256": "7ad8d57459782b70809da479380584a57cf259c66d9ff286811c0248b02732d2",
    "regulation_does_not_itself_define_RDF_owner_classes": true,
    "source_review": {
      "verification": "REVIEWED_SOURCE_FORMATTING_OR_NOTATION_RECONCILIATION",
      "source_path": "/Users/sadisfaction570/Desktop/Journal 1/NLTL_v2/MVP/evaluation_audit/source_review/IACS_I2_full.txt",
      "source_sha256": "7ad8d57459782b70809da479380584a57cf259c66d9ff286811c0248b02732d2",
      "line_start": 453,
      "line_end": 465,
      "excerpt": "         In the case of longitudinally-framed plating (  20 deg), when b < s, the net thickness is\n         given by:\n\n             tnet = 500 ꞏ s ꞏ ((AF ꞏ PPFp ꞏ Pavg) / y)0.5 ꞏ (2 ꞏ b / s – (b / s)2)0.5 / (1 + s / (2 ꞏ l)) [mm]\n\n\n         In the case of obliquely-framed plating (70 deg >  > 20 deg), linear interpolation is to be\n         used.\n\n             where  = smallest angle between the chord of the waterline and the line of the first\n                   level framing as illustrated in Figure 3 [deg].\n                   s = transverse frame spacing in transversely-framed ships or longitudinal frame\n                   spacing in longitudinally-framed ships [m]",
      "review_note": "Longitudinal <=20 degrees, b>=s and b<s branches and square-root term match; declared complex-readiness scope.",
      "frozen_text": "In the case of longitudinally-framed plating (Omega <= 20 deg), when b >= s, the net thickness is t_net = 500*s*sqrt((AF*PPF_p*P_avg)/sigma_y)/(1 + s/(2*l)) [mm]. When b < s, the net thickness is t_net = 500*s*sqrt((AF*PPF_p*P_avg)/sigma_y)*sqrt(2*b/s - (b/s)^2)/(1 + s/(2*l)) [mm]."
    },
    "source_location_status": "PREVIOUS_REVIEWED_EQUIVALENT_CLAUSE"
  },
